		<li id="comment-369142" class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1">
			<article class="comment-body" id="div-comment-369142"  itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" itemscope>
				<footer class="comment-meta" aria-label="Comment meta">
										<div class="comment-author-info">
						<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope>
							<cite itemprop="name" class="fn">Wendye</cite>						</div>

													<div class="entry-meta comment-metadata">
								<a href="https://www.softwaretestinghelp.com/agile-scrum-methodology-for-development-and-testing/#comment-369142">									<time datetime="2024-07-14T00:28:00+00:00" itemprop="datePublished">
										July 14, 2024 at 12:28 am									</time>
								</a>							</div>
												</div>

									</footer>

				<div class="comment-content" itemprop="text">
					<p>A really helpful article! The Agile Scrum methodology is gaining widespread popularity among the development as well as the testing teams across the globe due to its many advantages.</p>
<p>In fact, the new JIRA test management tools designed for automated web application testing are really helpful to agile teams. QARA Enterprise is an example of such a tool.</p>
<span class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-369142" data-commentid="369142" data-postid="3865" data-belowelement="div-comment-369142" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Wendye" aria-label="Reply to Wendye">Reply</a></span>				</div>
			</article>
			</li><!-- #comment-## -->

		<li id="comment-239145" class="comment even thread-even depth-1">
			<article class="comment-body" id="div-comment-239145"  itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" itemscope>
				<footer class="comment-meta" aria-label="Comment meta">
										<div class="comment-author-info">
						<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope>
							<cite itemprop="name" class="fn">Akshaya</cite>						</div>

													<div class="entry-meta comment-metadata">
								<a href="https://www.softwaretestinghelp.com/agile-scrum-methodology-for-development-and-testing/#comment-239145">									<time datetime="2024-07-11T10:41:30+00:00" itemprop="datePublished">
										July 11, 2024 at 10:41 am									</time>
								</a>							</div>
												</div>

									</footer>

				<div class="comment-content" itemprop="text">
					<p>This article help me gain clear idea about Agile methodology.Thanks a lot</p>
<span class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-239145" data-commentid="239145" data-postid="3865" data-belowelement="div-comment-239145" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Akshaya" aria-label="Reply to Akshaya">Reply</a></span>				</div>
			</article>
			</li><!-- #comment-## -->

		<li id="comment-353391" class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1">
			<article class="comment-body" id="div-comment-353391"  itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" itemscope>
				<footer class="comment-meta" aria-label="Comment meta">
										<div class="comment-author-info">
						<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope>
							<cite itemprop="name" class="fn">Shilpa Chatterjee Roy</cite>						</div>

													<div class="entry-meta comment-metadata">
								<a href="https://www.softwaretestinghelp.com/agile-scrum-methodology-for-development-and-testing/#comment-353391">									<time datetime="2024-07-11T08:51:10+00:00" itemprop="datePublished">
										July 11, 2024 at 8:51 am									</time>
								</a>							</div>
												</div>

									</footer>

				<div class="comment-content" itemprop="text">
					<p>Many of you have asked, why use Fibonacci series? Well in Fibonacci series, the next number is 60% more than the previous number so it helps to relatively estimate and size a story.</p>
<span class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-353391" data-commentid="353391" data-postid="3865" data-belowelement="div-comment-353391" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Shilpa Chatterjee Roy" aria-label="Reply to Shilpa Chatterjee Roy">Reply</a></span>				</div>
			</article>
			</li><!-- #comment-## -->

		<li id="comment-493025" class="comment even thread-even depth-1">
			<article class="comment-body" id="div-comment-493025"  itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" itemscope>
				<footer class="comment-meta" aria-label="Comment meta">
										<div class="comment-author-info">
						<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope>
							<cite itemprop="name" class="fn">Rakshatha</cite>						</div>

													<div class="entry-meta comment-metadata">
								<a href="https://www.softwaretestinghelp.com/agile-scrum-methodology-for-development-and-testing/#comment-493025">									<time datetime="2024-07-06T08:23:15+00:00" itemprop="datePublished">
										July 6, 2024 at 8:23 am									</time>
								</a>							</div>
												</div>

									</footer>

				<div class="comment-content" itemprop="text">
					<p>The tutorial is very detailed and helpful to beginners and experienced professionals alike.</p>
<span class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-493025" data-commentid="493025" data-postid="3865" data-belowelement="div-comment-493025" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Rakshatha" aria-label="Reply to Rakshatha">Reply</a></span>				</div>
			</article>
			</li><!-- #comment-## -->

		<li id="comment-302501" class="comment odd alt thread-odd thread-alt depth-1">
			<article class="comment-body" id="div-comment-302501"  itemtype="https://schema.org/Comment" itemscope>
				<footer class="comment-meta" aria-label="Comment meta">
										<div class="comment-author-info">
						<div class="comment-author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope>
							<cite itemprop="name" class="fn">KastorTroy</cite>						</div>

													<div class="entry-meta comment-metadata">
								<a href="https://www.softwaretestinghelp.com/agile-scrum-methodology-for-development-and-testing/#comment-302501">									<time datetime="2024-06-24T09:35:31+00:00" itemprop="datePublished">
										June 24, 2024 at 9:35 am									</time>
								</a>							</div>
												</div>

									</footer>

				<div class="comment-content" itemprop="text">
					<p>Nice job, but you mentioned that user stories should be sized using fibonacci numbers, but in the Burn Down Chart if I sum the 3 tasks of the user story 1, column Start; the total is 8+6+3 = 17, and that&#8217;s not a fibonacci number. I don&#8217;t understand</p>
<span class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-302501" data-commentid="302501" data-postid="3865" data-belowelement="div-comment-302501" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to KastorTroy" aria-label="Reply to KastorTroy">Reply</a></span>				</div>
			</article>
